* START-HISTORY:
* 14 Nov 26 Windows port - RELEASE_1.1 202: it answered "off" every time (@SDSYS has backslashes, @DS is '/'; measured in the VM), so
*   SDRADMIN was refused at sign-in while remote administration was open.  The state directory is found with either slash.
* 13 Nov 26 Windows port - written for RELEASE_1.1 202 (remote administration over ssh, Linux S.106's remote.sdsys in the Windows form).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    open = radmin_open(0)
*
*    @true when <ProgramData>\SD\remote-admin\state says "on", @false otherwise - no file, no directory, anything else in it.
*
*    The state is written by remote-admin.ps1 alone, in a directory only SYSTEM and Administrators may change and sdusers may read, so
*    LOGIN can read it as SDRADMIN (its one caller that is not elevated).  It is the fifth wall: LOGIN lands SDRADMIN only while it is on,
*    and DELETE.ACCOUNT leaves SDRADMIN alone while it is on.  FAIL CLOSED: anything that cannot be read is "off".
*
*    The place is the PARENT of the SDSYS directory, which is <ProgramData>\SD on every install (sd.iss DataDir), named from @sdsys
*    rather than from the environment, which the caller sets.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function radmin_open(arg)
$catalog !radmin_open

   open = @false
* 14 Nov 26 Windows port - RELEASE_1.1 202: @SDSYS is C:\ProgramData\SD\sdsys (backslashes) and @DS is '/' (measured in the VM), so
*   count(@sdsys, @ds) was 0 and this answered "off" every time: SDRADMIN was refused at sign-in with remote administration open.
*   The parent is found with either slash; Windows takes C:/... as well as C:\....
   sp = convert(char(92), '/', @sdsys)
   n = count(sp, '/')
   if n < 1 then return open
   state.dir = sp[1, index(sp, '/', n) - 1] : '/remote-admin'
   openpath state.dir to state.f then
      read state.rec from state.f, 'state' then
         if trim(state.rec<1>) = 'on' then open = @true
      end
      close state.f
   end

return open
end

* END-CODE
